WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.440
Map data from its source to every processor, queue, cache, log, and backup.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.369
Label trust boundaries where information moves between user devices, local servers, gateways,

00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:12.834
cloud accounts, providers, and third-party APIs.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:17.352
For each crossing, record the data class, purpose, recipient, encryption, retention,

00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:18.584
and authorized identities.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:22.692
A diagram is valuable only when it reflects runtime behavior.

00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:25.978
Prompt filtering can block prohibited fields, detect secrets,

00:00:25.978 --> 00:00:30.496
or redact identifiers before external use, but it is not infallible.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:34.193
Documents may reveal sensitive information through retrieved passages, filenames,

00:00:34.193 --> 00:00:35.836
embedded metadata, or summaries.

00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:41.587
Test filters against realistic inputs and define a safe action when classification is uncertain.

00:00:41.587 --> 00:00:45.284
Some data should never enter an automatic cloud route.

00:00:45.284 --> 00:00:48.981
Logs deserve the same classification as prompts and outputs.

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.856
Gateways, model servers, tracing tools, application telemetry,

00:00:51.856 --> 00:00:57.196
and provider consoles may record content, tokens, account identifiers, errors, and tool calls.

00:00:57.196 --> 00:01:00.893
Minimize content logging, restrict access, encrypt transport and storage,

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.536
and set retention intentionally.

00:01:02.536 --> 00:01:09.108
Confirm provider data-use and deletion terms rather than assuming an API request disappears after the response.

00:01:09.108 --> 00:01:14.448
Enforce policy close to the routing decision and again at destination access controls.

00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:19.377
Maintain evidence of which route processed a request without retaining unnecessary content.

00:01:19.377 --> 00:01:24.306
Review data flows when a model, provider, plugin, or observability tool changes.

00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:28.825
Hybrid privacy depends on controlling copies and metadata throughout the path,

00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:31.700
not merely keeping the original document local.
